          "title": "You'll want to know: نصح",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "نصح — naṣaḥa — \"to advise\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "نصحني الطبيب بالراحة. naṣaḥanī aṭ-ṭabīb bi-r-rāḥa. The doctor advised me to rest."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Present: ينصح, yanṣaḥ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The advice comes after بـ or أن: نصحه بـ …, نصحه أن …."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "نصح (naṣaḥa) is built on the native Arabic root n-ṣ-ḥ, \"to be sincere\" (Lane). Naṣaḥa is a Form I verb: to give sincere counsel, to advise."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
